     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg per day under medical supervision, or 1,200 mg per day over the counter. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the typical 400\u2013800 mg per dose.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician with prescribing authority for this patient. I can't enter one on behalf of the finance office.\n\nIf the order is meant for a real patient, the prescribing clinician should confirm the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, not exceeding 3,200 mg per day. That clinician can then enter the order, or ask me to enter it with the corrected dose."
      }
     ],
